In a strain gauge, the increase in resistance $\Delta R$ depends on the increase in length $\Delta L$. The variation of $\Delta R$ with $\Delta L$ is shown in Fig. 7.1.

{{figure:9702_m17_42_q07_figure_7_1}}

The strain gauge is connected into a circuit incorporating an ideal operational amplifier (op-amp), as shown in Fig. 7.2.

{{figure:9702_m17_42_q07_figure_7_2}}
